OL,3,AKing calls slave trade a 'shameful
OL,4,Achapter' during Commonwealth address
OL,5,
OL,6,FKing Charles has described the
OL,7,Ftransatlantic slave trade as a
OL,8,F"shameful chapter of history" that
OL,9,Ffilled him with "profound sorrow" as he
OL,10,Fopened a summit of Commonwealth leaders
OL,11,Fin the Caribbean.
OL,13,FHe said the trade in enslaved persons
OL,14,F"still casts a shadow" over the
OL,15,Fassociation of nations.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,304,300,200,140,0,100
PN,11906
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F119A1793732143
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs15j 5ws
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AKing calls slave trade a 'shameful
OL,4,Achapter' during Commonwealth address
OL,5,
OL,6,FThere has been calls from some for the
OL,7,FUK to make a formal apology for its
OL,8,Fhistoric role in the slave trade ahead
OL,9,Fof the Commonwealth Heads of Government
OL,10,FMeeting (Chogm) in Antigua and Barbuda,
OL,11,Fbut there was not one in the King's
OL,12,Faddress.
OL,14,FPrime Minister Andy Burnham, who is
OL,15,Falso at the summit, has previously said
OL,16,Fhe is open to Britain issuing a formal
OL,17,Fapology but that financial reparations
OL,18,Fwere "not the right answer".
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG6/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
